I"Ç<p>This post prepares a few examples on running jobs on the <a href="https://chtc.cs.wisc.edu">Center for High Throughout Computing (CHTC)</a> at UW-Madison.</p>

<h2 id="i-getting-started">I. Getting Started</h2>
<ol start="1">
  <li> Request an account.</li>
  <li> Log in.</li>
</ol>

<figure class="highlight"><pre><code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash">ssh username@ap2002.chtc.wisc.edu</code></pre></figure>

<ol start="3">
  <li>  Write two files: a submit file including submit information and a bash script to execuate your job.</li>
</ol>

<figure class="highlight"><pre><code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"><span class="c"># r_example.submit</span>
<span class="nv">universe</span><span class="o">=</span>docker
<span class="nv">docker_image</span><span class="o">=</span>xinranmiao/r_example:20221006
<span class="nv">log</span><span class="o">=</span>r_example.log
<span class="nv">error</span><span class="o">=</span>r_example.err
<span class="nv">output</span><span class="o">=</span>r_example.out
<span class="nv">executable</span><span class="o">=</span>r_example.sh
<span class="nv">request_disk</span><span class="o">=</span>1GB
queue</code></pre></figure>

<figure class="highlight"><pre><code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"><span class="c"># r_example.sh</span>
<span class="c">#!/bin/bash</span>
R <span class="nt">-e</span> <span class="s2">"installed.packages()"</span></code></pre></figure>

<ol start="4">
  <li>  Submit your job.</li>
</ol>

<figure class="highlight"><pre><code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash">condor_submit r_example.submit</code></pre></figure>

<ol start="5">
  <li>  (Optional) Check your job and/or edit it.</li>
</ol>

<figure class="highlight"><pre><code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"><span class="c"># query your jobs</span>
condor_q
<span class="c"># you'll find your job_id, say it's 9644580 </span>

<span class="c"># query jobs on hold</span>
condor_q <span class="nt">-hold</span>

<span class="c"># analyze a job (e.g., why a job keeps idle)</span>
condor_q <span class="nt">-better-analyze</span> 9644580 

<span class="c"># log into a job</span>
condor_ssh_to_job <span class="nt">-auto-retry</span> 9644580 

<span class="c"># change requested resources</span>
<span class="c"># use it when a job is held due to insufficient resources</span>
condor_qedit 9644580 RequestMemory 2200

<span class="c"># remove a job</span>
condor_rm 9644580 </code></pre></figure>

<h2 id="ii-parallel-jobs">II. Parallel Jobs</h2>
<h3 id="example-1-run-multiple-jobs">Example 1: Run Multiple Jobs</h3>
<p>Suppose you wish to run 20 jobs, you may change the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">queue</code> in <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">r_example.submit</code> to be <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">queue 20</code>.</p>

<figure class="highlight"><pre><code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"><span class="c"># r_example.submit</span>
<span class="nv">universe</span><span class="o">=</span>docker
<span class="nv">docker_image</span><span class="o">=</span>xinranmiao/r_example:20221006

<span class="nv">log</span><span class="o">=</span>r_example<span class="si">$(</span>Process<span class="si">)</span>.log
<span class="nv">error</span><span class="o">=</span>r_example<span class="si">$(</span>Process<span class="si">)</span>.err
<span class="nv">output</span><span class="o">=</span>r_example<span class="si">$(</span>Process<span class="si">)</span>.out

<span class="nv">executable</span><span class="o">=</span>r_example.sh

<span class="nv">request_disk</span><span class="o">=</span>1GB
queue 20</code></pre></figure>

<h3 id="example-2-read-arguments-from-file">Example 2: Read Arguments from File</h3>
<p>Suppose one wishes to read arguments from <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">args.txt</code> in order to run an R file <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">run.R</code> taking several input arguments.</p>

<figure class="highlight"><pre><code class="language-r" data-lang="r"><span class="c1"># run.R</span><span class="w">
</span><span class="n">opts</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">&lt;-</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">commandArgs</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">trailingOnly</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="kc">TRUE</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="w">
</span><span class="n">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">opts</span><span class="p">)</span></code></pre></figure>

<figure class="highlight"><pre><code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"><span class="c"># args.txt</span>
1,3,100
2,3,200</code></pre></figure>

<p>Then we can modify the last line of the submit file so that it reads from the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">args.txt</code>. Remember to transfer both <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">args.txt</code> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">run.R</code> by setting <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">transfer_input_files</code>.</p>

<figure class="highlight"><pre><code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"><span class="c"># parallel_example.submit</span>
<span class="nv">universe</span><span class="o">=</span>docker
<span class="nv">docker_image</span><span class="o">=</span>xinranmiao/r_example:20221006
<span class="nv">log</span><span class="o">=</span>parallel_example<span class="si">$(</span>job_id<span class="si">)</span>.log
<span class="nv">error</span><span class="o">=</span>parallel_example<span class="si">$(</span>job_id<span class="si">)</span>.err
<span class="nv">output</span><span class="o">=</span>parallel_example<span class="si">$(</span>job_id<span class="si">)</span>.out

<span class="nv">executable</span><span class="o">=</span>parallel_example.sh
<span class="nv">arguments</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="si">$(</span>job_id<span class="si">)</span> <span class="si">$(</span>n<span class="si">)</span> <span class="si">$(</span>d<span class="si">)</span>

<span class="nv">transfer_input_files</span><span class="o">=</span>args.txt, run.R

<span class="nv">request_cpus</span><span class="o">=</span>1
<span class="nv">request_memory</span><span class="o">=</span>1GB
<span class="nv">request_disk</span><span class="o">=</span>2GB
<span class="nv">requirements</span><span class="o">=(</span>has_avx <span class="o">==</span> <span class="nb">true</span><span class="o">)</span>

queue job_id, d, n from args.txt</code></pre></figure>

<p>We may also update the bash script so that it runs the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">run.R</code> file.</p>

<figure class="highlight"><pre><code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"><span class="c"># parallel_example.sh</span>
<span class="c">#!/bin/bash</span>
Rscript run.R <span class="nv">$2</span> <span class="nv">$3</span></code></pre></figure>

<h2 id="iii-environment">III. Environment</h2>
<h3 id="docker-images">Docker Images</h3>
<p>The CHTC supports using pulling docker images; see their <a href="https://chtc.cs.wisc.edu/uw-research-computing/docker-jobs.html">documentation</a>. In fact, all the examples above used a toy docker image I made from <a href="https://github.com/XinranMiao/docker_chtc_example/blob/main/R_example/Dockerfile">this dockerfile</a>. You may find some toy examples for R and python from <a href="https://github.com/XinranMiao/docker_chtc_example">my earlier repo</a>.</p>

<h3 id="installing-packages">Installing Packages</h3>
<p>There are official tutorials on running <a href="https://chtc.cs.wisc.edu/uw-research-computing/r-jobs.html">R</a>, <a href="https://chtc.cs.wisc.edu/uw-research-computing/julia-jobs.html">Julia</a>, <a href="https://chtc.cs.wisc.edu/uw-research-computing/python-jobs.html">Python</a>, and others on CHTC.</p>

